Hi Bernadette,

I've attached a one-page explanation for the advisers to use at the first app=
ointment. You could read the introduction aloud and pause for questions.

There are eight sessions. In the room, learners will read an invitation with =
the tutor, following its headings to find what to bring and where to meet. Th=
ey can point to the words that helped them answer.

If someone misses a session, we'll post the paper for that session. They can =
start with the notice, work through the questions and use the check section t=
o compare their answers with the notice; they won't need a device. The reply =
slip in the material is for practice and does not need to be sent in. Please =
confirm the application to attend the course separately with the person at th=
e Ashford appointment.

I hope that gives your team a clear starting point.

Thanks,
Heather

On Mon, 10 Feb 2025 at 09:32, Bernadette McLean wrote:
> Hi Heather,
>
> Our advisers will begin speaking with people about Everyday Document Basics=
. Could you give us a short explanation we can read aloud at the first referr=
al appointment?
>
> What will people read together with the tutor? If someone misses a session =
and does not have a device, where do they start with the material sent home? =
And is the reply slip in the learning material something they really need to =
submit?
>
> It would help us to make the distinction clear before anyone takes the pape=
rs away.
>
> Thanks,
> Bernadette


